---
title: Sausage, kale & gnocchi one-pot
servings: 4
course: dinner
tags: quick, one-pan, pork, potato
image: https://images.immediate.co.uk/production/volatile/sites/30/2020/08/sausage-kale-gnocchi-one-pot-e890b33.jpg?resize=440,400
source: https://www.bbcgoodfood.com/recipes/sausage-kale-gnocchi-one-pot
prep time: 5m
cook time: 15m
---

Heat the @olive oil{1%tbsp} in a large high-sided #frying pan{} over a medium heat. Squeeze the @pork sausage{6} straight from their skins into the pan, then use the back of a wooden spoon to break the meat up. Sprinkle in the @chilli flake{1%tsp} and @?fennel seed{1%tsp}, if using, then fry until the sausagemeat is crisp around the edges. Remove from the pan with a slotted spoon.

Tip the @gnocchi{500%g} into the pan, fry for ~{1%minute} or so, then pour in the @chicken stock{500%ml}. Once bubbling, cover the pan with a #lid{} and cook for ~{3%minutes}, then stir in the @kale{100%g}(chopped). Cook for ~{2%minutes} more or until the gnocchi is tender and the kale has wilted. Stir in the @parmesan{40%g}(finely grated), then season with black pepper and scatter the crisp sausagemeat over the top.
